/T (The results should not be interpreted as one algorithm being better than the other. The algorithms solve different objectives. Kruskal is appropriate when the requirement is minimum-cost network connectivity, whereas Dijkstra is appropriate when the requirement is minimum-cost routing from a source. The graphical outputs make the difference between the complete graph, the selected MST, and the shortest route directly observable.)
