687 0 obj
<<
/Title (The implementation successfully demonstrates the difference between two important greedy graph optimization problems. Kruskal's algorithm constructs a Minimum Spanning Tree with total cost 4, connecting all five vertices using four selected edges. Dijkstra's algorithm finds the shortest path from A to E with cost 3.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 588 0 R
/Next 688 0 R
>>
endobj
688 0 obj
<<
/Title (The results should not be interpreted as one algorithm being better than the other. The algorithms solve different objectives. Kruskal is appropriate when the requirement is minimum-cost network connectivity, whereas Dijkstra is appropriate when the requirement is minimum-cost routing from a source. The graphical outputs make the difference between the complete graph, the selected MST, and the shortest route directly observable.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 588 0 R
/Prev 687 0 R
>>
endobj
